            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Pakistan-based agencies (median rates, 2026)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>SEO retainer:</strong> PKR 60K-300K / month (USD 215-1,075)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Google Ads management:</strong> PKR 50K-200K / month (USD 180-720) + ad spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Meta Ads management:</strong> PKR 50K-200K / month (USD 180-720) + ad spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Social media management:</strong> PKR 40K-150K / month (USD 145-540)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Full-service retainer:</strong> PKR 200K-800K / month (USD 720-2,870)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>One-time SEO audit:</strong> PKR 50K-200K (USD 180-720)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Landing page (with copy + design):</strong> PKR 80K-300K (USD 290-1,075)</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">USA-based agencies (median rates, 2026)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>SEO retainer:</strong> USD 1,500-10,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Google Ads management:</strong> USD 1,000-5,000 / month + ad spend (often 10-20% of spend)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Meta Ads management:</strong> USD 1,000-5,000 / month + ad spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Social media management:</strong> USD 800-4,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Full-service retainer:</strong> USD 3,000-25,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>One-time SEO audit:</strong> USD 2,000-15,000</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Landing page:</strong> USD 1,500-8,000</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">UK-based agencies (median rates, 2026)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>SEO retainer:</strong> GBP 1,200-6,000 / month (USD 1,500-7,500)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>PPC management:</strong> GBP 800-4,000 / month + spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Social media management:</strong> GBP 600-3,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Full-service retainer:</strong> GBP 2,500-15,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>SEO audit:</strong> GBP 1,500-8,000</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">UAE-based agencies (median rates, 2026)</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>SEO retainer:</strong> AED 3,500-15,000 / month (USD 950-4,100)</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>PPC management:</strong> AED 3,000-12,000 / month + spend</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Social media management:</strong> AED 2,500-10,000 / month</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Full-service retainer:</strong> AED 10,000-50,000 / month</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What you actually pay for</h2>
              <p>Most clients underestimate the labor inside a marketing retainer. A 'USD 2,000/month <a href="/services/seo-services/" style="text-decoration:underline;">SEO</a> retainer' is roughly 30-40 hours of senior strategist time — including keyword research, technical audits, content briefs, link-outreach, and monthly reporting. Once you split that across 4 weeks, you're getting about 8 hours of senior attention per week. That's a fair trade for the work, but not magic.</p>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Strategy and planning:</strong> 15-25% of retainer hours</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Execution (writing, optimizing, designing):</strong> 50-60%</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Reporting and account management:</strong> 15-25%</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Tools and software costs:</strong> typically rolled into the retainer (Ahrefs, Semrush, etc.)</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">What drives cost up or down</h2>
              <ul style="line-height:1.8;padding-left:20px;margin:20px 0;"><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Industry compliance:</strong> healthcare, finance, and legal advertising are more expensive due to regulatory overhead</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Multi-language campaigns:</strong> add 30-50% per additional language</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Geographic reach:</strong> single-city vs national vs international shifts costs significantly</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Reporting depth:</strong> custom dashboards add 10-20% to retainer</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Ad spend size:</strong> agencies often charge 10-15% of ad spend as their management fee on Google/Meta Ads</li><li style="margin-bottom:10px;"><strong>Seniority:</strong> a senior strategist at USD 80/hr vs a junior at USD 25/hr drives most of the price differential</li></ul>
              <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4">Why Apex Marketings prices the way we do</h2>
              <p>We're a Rawalpindi-based agency that serves clients in Pakistan, USA, UK, and UAE. Our rates sit at the bottom of the US/UK ranges and the top of the Pakistan ranges — reflecting that we deliver to international standards but operate from Pakistan's cost base. Our typical retainer client pays USD 800-3,500/month for a full-service mix; one-off projects start at USD 600.</p>
              <p>We publish <a href="../../pricing/">starting-from prices on our pricing page</a> because hiding pricing wastes everyone's time.</p>
            <h2 class="cs-font_36 mb-4 mt-5">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Why is digital marketing so expensive?</h3><p>Most of the cost is human labor — senior strategists, copywriters, ad-buyers, and analysts. Tools (Ahrefs, Semrush, Meta Business Manager training) are real but small relative to people costs. The 'value' of a good marketer is they spend your ad budget more efficiently — usually saving 20-40% versus running it yourself.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Can I do marketing in-house cheaper?</h3><p>Sometimes. If you have a junior marketer + good external help, you can match agency output for less. The catch: most in-house marketers struggle without senior strategy oversight, and most founders burn out trying to learn paid ads while running their business.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">How do I avoid getting overcharged?</h3><p>Three rules: (1) get 3 quotes, (2) demand a written scope of deliverables and KPIs, (3) pay monthly with a 30-day exit clause for the first 90 days. Any agency that refuses these is hiding something.</p>
              <h3 class="cs-font_24 mt-4 mb-2">Is Pakistan-based marketing as good as US/UK?</h3><p>Yes, at the top tier. We work with the same tools (Google Ads, Meta Ads Manager, Ahrefs, Semrush), follow the same playbooks, and read the same Twitter / LinkedIn marketers as US/UK agencies. The gap is geography and time zone, not quality.</p>
